This is a known breaking change. Android deprecated `AdjustResize` (API 30+), and .NET 10 MAUI defaults to **edge-to-edge** rendering, which ignores the old `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` behavior.

Here's what to do instead:

### 1. Use `Padding` bound to keyboard insets (recommended)

In your `MauiProgram.cs`, keep edge-to-edge and react to insets:

```csharp
// No special builder config needed — edge-to-edge is the default in .NET 10
```

Then in your chat page, wrap your input bar so it respects the keyboard inset. On **Android**, subscribe to inset changes in a platform-specific handler:

```csharp
// ChatPage.xaml.cs
#if ANDROID
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Platform;
#endif

protected override void OnAppearing()
{
    base.OnAppearing();
#if ANDROID
    var activity = Platform.CurrentActivity;
    var rootView = activity?.Window?.DecorView?.RootView;
    if (rootView is not null)
    {
        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(rootView, new KeyboardInsetsListener(InputBar));
    }
#endif
}
```

```csharp
#if ANDROID
class KeyboardInsetsListener(View inputBar) : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

        // Use the larger of keyboard or nav bar bottom inset
        var bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom);
        var density = v.Context?.Resources?.DisplayMetrics?.Density ?? 1;

        inputBar.Margin = new Thickness(0, 0, 0, bottom / density);
        return insets;
    }
}
#endif
```

### 2. Quick-and-dirty fallback

If you just want the old resize behavior back, you can force it per-activity in `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using Android.Views;

protected override void OnCreate(Bundle? savedInstanceState)
{
    base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);
    // Opt out of edge-to-edge and restore legacy resize
    Window?.SetSoftInputMode(SoftInput.AdjustResize);
}
```

> ⚠️ This fights the edge-to-edge default and may break on future Android versions. Prefer option 1 for production apps.

### On iOS

iOS already adjusts layout for the keyboard by default in MAUI. If you still see overlap, set `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll.Disconnect()` isn't called, and ensure your `Entry`/`Editor` is inside a `ScrollView` or use the built-in `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll`.

**TL;DR:** The modern fix is to listen to `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` and adjust your input bar's margin/padding accordingly. The old `AdjustResize` API is deprecated.
